From: hans2294 <22217531+hans2294@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 02:41:10 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] wsi: present headless surfaces into Haiku views

A headless surface created with VkHaikuViewSurfaceCreateInfoHAIKU
(vulkan_haiku.h) gets CPU images (a GPU blit to a linear buffer), the
view's size and BGRA formats, and each present waits for the blit and
draws the rows into the view through a BBitmap, with the window locked.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
